      <Comment source="pmngroup">The |FRAME: G-5283 DTS2| gene isolated from |FRAME: TAX-4530 &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt;| encodes an |FRAME: MONOMER-6803 9&amp;beta;-pimara-7,15-diene synthase| |CITS:[15299118]|. This recombinant enzyme expressed as a GST-fusion in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; was shown to convert |FRAME: CPD-8719 9&amp;alpha;-copalyl diphosphate| into |FRAME: CPD-4754 (-)-9&amp;beta;-pimara-7,15-diene|, a putative diterpene hydrocarbon precursor of the phytoalexin/allochemical momilactones. It was reported that the plastidial transit peptide hinders folding of the full-length protein when expressed &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS:[15299118]|. Please note: This enzyme is from |FRAME: TAX-39946|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-6803" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phytozome" value="Os04t0179700-01" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Modbase" value="Q66QH3" />
