    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-13866" textLabel="MONOMER-13866" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q2PHF2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="517.771240234375" centerY="423.74713134765625" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">The |FRAME: G-10580 OsKS5| gene of |FRAME: TAX-39947 &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt; Japonica Group| has been cloned, and a GST-fusion was expressed and purified. The recombinant enzyme was shown to catalyze a |FRAME: MONOMER-13866 &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-pimara-8(14),15-diene synthase| reaction |CITS: [16861806]|. While |FRAME: CPD-7097 &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-pimara-8(14),15-diene| is known to be produced as a minor product by the enzyme |FRAME: MONOMER-11970 &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-sandaracopimaradiene synthase|, encoded by |FRAME: G-9282 KS10|, it is the sole product of this enzyme. The purpose of |FRAME: CPD-7097 &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-pimara-8(14),15-diene| is still unknown, though it has been established that it is not a precursor in the biosynthesis of either gibberellins or phytoalexins |CITS: [16861806]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-13866" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phytozome" value="Os02t0571300-01" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q2PHF2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-14824" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="Os02t0571300-01" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="G-10580" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="87.724" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightSeq" value="87.724" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_KANNO06" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-18613" textLabel="9β-pimara-7,15-diene oxidase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q0JF01" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="475.950927734375" centerY="651.767822265625" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="O-28, hartmut">Utilizing the recoded and N-terminally modified gene of CYP999A3 from &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt; and expressing the rCYP99A3 in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; the molecular function of the cytochrome P450 dependent CYP99A3 as a 9&amp;beta;-pimara-7,15-diene oxidase has been demonstrated. CYP99A3 catalyzes the sequential oxidation of the C-19 methyl group of |FRAME:CPD-4754 (-)-9&amp;beta;-pimara-7,15-diene| to yield |FRAME:CPD-13923 (-)-9&amp;beta;-pimara-7,15-dien-19-oate|. Those oxidation steps include the transient formation of an diterpenoid alcohol (|FRAME:CPD-13921 (-)-9&amp;beta;-pimara-7,15-dien-19-ol|), an diterpenoid aldehyde (|FRAME:CPD-13922 (-)-9&amp;beta;-pimara-7,15-dien-19-al|) and finally the diterpenoid carboxylic acid ||FRAME:CPD-13923 (-)-9&amp;beta;-pimara-7,15-dien-19-oate|), considered an early intermediate in the |FRAME:CPD-7092 momilactone A| synthesis which is supported by its natural occurrence in &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt;. In addition, the C19 transformation appears to be a requirement towards the formation of the 19,6-&amp;gamma;-lactone ring which not only finalizes the core structure of |FRAME:CPD-1092 styrene| but is also eponymous for the compound |CITS:[21175892]|. The involvement of CYP99A3 had already been indicated by the strong suppression of momilactone biosynthesis when CYP99A3 was knocked-out in &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt; |CITS:[17872948]|. CYP99A3 was also able to catalyze the same oxidation sequence with |FRAME:CPD-9907 9&amp;beta;-stemod-13(17)-ene| to form |FRAME:CPD-16681 9&amp;beta;-stemod-13(17)-en-19-oate| via |FRAME:CPD-16679 9&amp;beta;-stemod-13(17)-en-19-ol| and |FRAME:CPD-16680 9&amp;beta;-stemod-13(17)-en-19-al|. Although those compounds have not yet been identified in &lt;i&gt;Oryza&lt;/i&gt; it might provide indication towards the metabolic fate of the ambiguous |FRAME:CPD-9907 9&amp;beta;-stemod-13(17)-ene| |CITS:[21175892]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-18613" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phytozome" value="Os04t0178400-01" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS00086" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prints" value="PR00463" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF00067" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR001128" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Gene3D" value="1.10.630.10" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q0JF01" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="BAG92737.1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-22715, RXN-22714, RXN-22713, RXN-22712, RXN-22711, RXN-22710, RXN-22709, RXN-22708" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="8" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="Os04t0178400-01" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="G-18078" />
